Z||000001||Pontiaddict||04-07-2001||05:25 PM||||If you lived outside the US, you could get it with an LS1. But the American versions of the Catera are getting the turbo 3.0L v6. Why? I don't know.<P>They are thinking about doing the V8 Impalla though, but with the AWD out of an Aztek.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Shaft||04-07-2001||06:58 PM||||I heard GM cancelled the Impala V8 project. I never heard about it having the AWD from the Aztec though. That was the Grand Prix G8 show car at the auto show this year. It had a 5.7 LS1 V8 with AWD. But there are no production plans for that car.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Slammed Fiero||04-07-2001||07:17 PM||||Official word from a friend at GM marketing (my former job) is that the V8 Impala was shelfed in favor of the 3800SC , as well we will never see the LS6 powered Fbody before their demise in 2002<P>According to a recent article by john moss concerning hot rod cadillacs is that the "Bean Counters" ie accountants don't see it happening anytime soon , the sport version is likley all you will ever see.. <P>JM ||||reg||1
